N|               The children rush inside!                                            
S|               INT. PIANO NOBILE. PALAZZO. NIGHT.                                   
O|
N|               The vast reception hall UNVEILED: The real life incarnation          
N|               of the puppets’ backdrop. The entire piano nobile DECORATED          
N|               SPOOKILY FOR A HALLOWE’EN PARTY. CANDLES line the GRAND              
N|               STAIRCASE. Pumpkins on every perch.                                  
O|
N|               The palazzo itself is ornate, graven, regal. Like a dying            
N,M|               monarchy.  Large windows (now streaked with RAIN).                   
O|
N|               A TABLE OF CARNIVAL MASKS. Classic styles, feathered, gilded         
N|               and graven. Bauta, Pantalone, Zanni, Gnaga... Columbinas             
N|               and Jokers... Ariadne puts a Capitano mask on Portfoglio. A          
N|               painted Romeo for herself. Poirot declines one.                      
O|
N,G|               SHOTS OF THE PARTY. GAMES.  GLORIOUS, GIGGLING CHAOS:                
N|               -- CHILDREN decorate BROOMS, prizes given to the best, as --         
O|
S|               INT. MUSIC ROOM. PALAZZO. NIGHT.                                     
O|
N|               A handsome rehearsal space decorated with opera memorabilia:         
