C|                                   POIROT                                           
U|                         Please understand, I would welcome with                    
U|                         open arms any honest sign of devil or                      
U|                         demon or ghost -- for if there is a ghost                  
U|                         there is a soul -- if there is a soul                      
U|                         there is a God who made it. And if we                      
U|                         have God, we have everything -- meaning,                   
U|                         order, justice. But I have seen too much                   
U|                         of the world. Countless crimes.  Two                       
U|                         wars.  The bitter evil of indifference.                    
U|                         And I conclude, no, no god, no ghosts --                   
U|                         no mediums who can speak to them --                        
